From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VIctory contributor <contributor@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 21:35:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/13] VICTORY_THREAD_TICKET=1: relabelled compute threads
 take their ids from a counter

Off by default; unset, nothing changes. Issue #1243: a compute program
with console lanes is relabelled so that its host lane is its console
lane: flat id = the wave's first flat id rounded down to the wave size,
plus the lane. That is a bijection only while each host wave holds a
wave-aligned run of flat ids. A host may fill a group of more than one
dimension from tiles instead (NVIDIA: 16 x 2 of a 32 x 2 group per
wave), so two waves round down to the same start: half the ids are given
twice and the other half never.

With the switch on, a program with console lanes that is not run in
halves, in a group of more than one wave and more than one dimension,
takes one more LDS dword. Every thread zeroes it, the group meets, and
the first lane of each wave adds its wave's share atomically:
- a full wave adds the wave size to the low 16 bits and takes the low
  bits it found as its first id (wave-aligned runs from 0 up, so host
  lanes stay console lanes),
- a wave that is not full adds its count to the high 16 bits and takes
  its ids from the group's end down: group - (found high + count).
A thread's id is its wave's first plus its rank in the wave. Each id of
the group is given once whatever the host puts in a wave, and none lies
outside the group, with any number of waves that are not full. In the
entry block, branch-free, as wave_base does for the halves; the halves
path (wave_base) is not touched.

Fork PR #1261 fixes the same issue and broke faces and hair on another
card; not taken. This is written anew: off by default, its own
function, and no assumption of one wave that is not full per group.

Measured on an RTX 3060 (ticket_card_tests, a wave32 program storing 1
at its thread id), ids given by the rounding: 32 x 2: 32 of 64;
32 x 8: 128 of 256; 64 x 4: 128 of 256; 24 x 8: 128 of 192;
12 x 12: 96 of 144; 10 x 10: 68 of 100; 8 x 8, 16 x 16, 64 x 1: all.
With tickets: every id of all nine groups, none outside.

Tests: ticket_tests (4, the arithmetic over made-up waves),
ticket_card_tests (2, on the card). Corpus (533, VICTORY_HOST_WAVE=32):
532 validated with the switch off and on (f133e35e fails as before).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
